  "selection": "One three-edge chain, edges (0,1), (1,2), (2,3). The block family is [(0,1),(1,2)] and [(1,2),(2,3)]. The blocks share (1,2), and every carrier edge sits in a block, so the family is an overlapping cover and not a partition. Five laws: the empty list; a prohibit of the shared edge (1,2) when (0,1) is present; a prohibit of (0,1) when (1,2) is present; a multiply by 3 of (1,2) when (2,3) is present; and a multiply by 3 of (2,3) when (0,1) is present. Those last two edges lie in different blocks. None of the four lists is an atlas-012 multiply. Each law is observed by four maps: the bare intersection graph of active blocks, the bare realised-overlap graph, the labelled realised blocks, and the count of present shared edges. The maps were named before execution. The family does not change over time.",
  "grammar": {
